  "query_preview": "range models are in good agreement with an H5 trough \ndigging southeast from the northern high Plains into the upper \nMidwest and MS River Valley. The stronger ascent ahead of the H5 \ntrough will cause scattered showers and thunderstorms to develop \nacross the CWA Friday afternoon into Friday night.\n\nSaturday through Tuesday:\n\nThe H5 ridge will shift east into the southern and central high \nPlains on Saturday and Sunday. The H5 ridge will flatten a bit and \nmid level perturbations will round the ridge axis Sunday through \nTuesday. There will be chances for for showers and thunderstorms \nSunday through Monday. A back door cold front will push southwest \nacross the CWA Monday afternoon as an H5 trough amplifies across the \neast central conus. The better chances for showers and thunderstorms\nwill shift south and west of the CWA on Tuesday. There will not be \nmuch of a cool down as high temperatures remain in the upper 80s to \nlower 90s.",
